start":"2026-11-24T18:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T18:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"STONE de Garance Maillot à La Balsamine : une pièce physique intense qui interroge la matière, la gravité et la relation des corps à la pierre. Festival Cuddles.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4442","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2102-stone-garance-maillot","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2103-une-tentative-presque-comme-une-autre-clement","title":"Une tentative presque comme une autre","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-24T19:15:00Z","end":"2026-11-27T22:15:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Clément & Guillaume Papachristou présentent une performance fraternelle et physique touchante au Théâtre National dans le cadre du festival Cuddles.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4443","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2103-une-tentative-presque-comme-une-autre-clement-guillaume-papachristou","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-theatre-varia-les-veilleuses","title":"Les Veilleuses","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w104994690","start":"2026-11-25T18:00:00Z","end":"2026-12-05T20:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Entre jeu masqué et constellations d’images évocatrices et poétiques, la nouvelle création d’Héloïse Meire se déploie comme un roman graphique porté à la scène, nous immergeant dans le quotidien des aidant·es proches","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://varia.be/sites/default/files/2026-05/visuel%20Les%20Veileuses%20verticalCMJN.jpg","sourceURL":"https://varia.be/programme/2026-2027/heloise-meire/les-veilleuses","sourceName":"Théâtre Varia","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":false,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-brigittines-wallpaper","title":"WALLPAPER: Astero Styliani Lamprinou","category":"dance","venueID":"osm-w260917265","start":"2026-11-25T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Motifs en mouvementsLes motifs des rouleaux de papiers peints qui décorent les intérieurs sont autant de marqueurs du temps qui passe, et touchent à notre Histoire sociale et esthétique. Chorégraphe, danseuse, performeuse, vidéaste, nourrie d’architecture et de surréalisme, Astero Styliani Lamprinou s’inspire d’imprimés datant du baroque aux seventies, en passant par les Années folles ou les années 1950, pour proposer une traversée du temps comme autant de mutations, comme autant de lés d’un papier peint qui change, s’accumule, se fragmente.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://brigittines.be/sites/default/files/2026-10/WALLPAPER%201%20%40Noor%20Jorquera%20Trascastro.JPG","sourceURL":"https://www.brigittines.be/fr/agenda/brigitte-en-novembre/wallpaper","sourceName":"Les Brigittines","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-brigittines-solar","title":"SOLAR: Delphine Friquet","category":"dance","venueID":"osm-w260917265","start":"2026-11-25T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Rester vivant·esLa beauté devient leur spectacle : celui de la Danseuse, celui du Musicien, et celui de Celle qui les éclaire. Ce sont trois interprètes, trois personnages qui fabriquent les images en direct, des images colorées, embrasées, solaires, comme autant d’instants présents voués à toucher à l’éternité.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://brigittines.be/sites/default/files/2026-08/SOLAR%20%40BarbaraSalom%C3%A9%203.jpg","sourceURL":"https://www.brigittines.be/fr/agenda/brigitte-en-novembre/solar","sourceName":"Les Brigittines","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700023745","title":"Festival Cinemamed 2026","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w1334658369","start":"2026-11-25T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-12-04T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Le festival Cinemamed (Festival cinéma méditerranéen de Bruxelles) est de retour du 26 novembre au 4 décembre au Cinéma Palace et au Cinéma Aventure pour une nouvelle édition immanquable! Quelques projections auront lieu aussi à l’Espace Magh, au Cinéma Galeries, à Bozar, au W:Halll, au RITCS et à la Cinematek ! C’est le rendez-vous de l’année pour découvrir une sélection de films de qualité reflétant les réalités sociales et culturelles de tout le bassin méditerranéen. Au programme de cette 26e édition : des documentaires percutants, des fictions inédites, des courts métrages, des avant-premières, des concerts et une multitude d’évènements qui font l’ambiance chaleureuse et conviviale du Cinemamed ! Depuis 1989, le Cinemamed promeut le vivre ensemble et met en avant des thématiques engagées. C’est aussi un forum de réflexion et de dialogue entre personnes et cultures. Venez rencontrer…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":1.25,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/22039f786b2c713be2f3270b0c275449af03aafa.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700023745","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2108-nez-noir-estelle-samira-borel","title":"NEZ NOIR","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-26T18:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T17:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Estelle Borel présente NEZ NOIR au Brass : une performance sur fil et en costume de mouton, acte poétique de résistance face aux stéréotypes. Festival Cuddles.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4447","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2108-nez-noir-estelle-samira-borel","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2107-people-claudio-stellato","title":"PEOPLE","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-26T19:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-27T22:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Découvrez PEOPLE de Claudio Stellato au Marni. Une performance physique absurde et drôle qui repousse les limites du corps et du mouvement. Festival Cuddles.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4446","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2107-people-claudio-stellato","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2105-anger-angels-eternal-letdown-sophia-rodriguez","title":"anger angels ETERNAL LETDOWN","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-26T19:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T20:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"anger angels ETERNAL LETDOWN par Sophia Rodriguez et Teresa Vittucci au Kaaitheater : une performance de résistance queer intense pour le festival Cuddles.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4445","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2105-anger-angels-eternal-letdown-sophia-rodriguez-teresa-vittucci","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2109-nocturne-parade-compagnie-non-nova-phia-menar","title":"Nocturne Parade","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-27T17:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-29T20:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Nocturne Parade de Phia Ménard aux Halles : un conte visuel entre vent, lumière et marionnettes pour résister à l'obscurité du monde. Un rendez-vous Cuddles.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4448","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2109-nocturne-parade-compagnie-non-nova-phia-menard","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":false,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"kanal-no-show","title":"NO SHOW","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-01-17T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Can a museum entertain? On the site of Brussels’ first luna park, artist duo Deborah Bowmann, musician Maoupa Mazzocchetti and 20 Brussels artists pose this question with a hint of irony. Their response takes shape in NO SHOW, where art, light, sound and performance converge in a fully immersive experience across five rooms. Rooted in the playful spirit of artist-run initiatives and in the structures that support them, NO SHOW explores how artists sustain their practices in a world increasingly geared towards quick pleasures, scattered attention and high consumption.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v7r3IAA.jpg?crop=5526%2C2891%2C0%2C553&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/no-show","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-joelle-tuerlinckx","title":"Joëlle Tuerlinckx","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"For several years, Joëlle Tuerlinckx kept a close eye on the construction of Kanal. With a light show and an explosive symphony of sounds co-created with Christoph Fink, she puts you under hypnosis and introduces you to the underground part of both the museum and her work. In the empty space, stories about foundations slowly blend with other tales.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v901IAA.jpg?crop=8256%2C4320%2C0%2C592&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/joelle-tuerlinckx","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-manon-de-boer","title":"Manon de Boer","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Amidst the bustle of the new museum and the city, Manon de Boer’s sound installation Blindsight invites you to slow down. Together with choreographer Latifa Laâbissi and sound designer Laszlo Umbreit, de Boer animates the voices of artists who inspire them, from Chantal Akerman to Beyoncé.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/2026-01/share.jpg?crop=1200%2C628%2C0%2C1&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/manon-de-boer","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-joshua-serafin","title":"Joshua Serafin","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Why do we continue searching for what has been lost? In Whispering Pleas of the eternal echoes, you are invited to join the search for Joshua Serafin’s roots. This immersive film installation weaves together scenes across countries and generations. In the artist’s unique cosmology, past and present enter into conversation.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v8FFIAY.jpg?crop=4672%2C2445%2C0%2C1799&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/joshua-serafin","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-596138","title":"Manon de Boer","category":"art","venueID":"v-a4450aabedab","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Au milieu de lʹagitation du nouveau musée, Blindsight vous invite à ralentir. Installez-vous dans un fauteuil de cinéma et laissez-vous transporter par la bande originale dʹun film que vous pouvez ressentir plutôt que voir. Cette installation de lʹartiste Manon de Boer, réalisée en collaboration avec la chorégraphe Latifa Laâbissi et le concepteur sonore Laszlo Umbreit, forme le dernier volet dʹun triptyque qui a commencé avec la performance Ghost Party 1 (2022), suivie par le film Ghost Party 2 (2022). Dans ce film, Manon de Boer et Latifa Laâbissi prêtent leurs voix à des artistes et des écrivain·es qui les ont inspirées, comme Chantal Akerman, Beyoncé, Anne Carson ou Marguerite Duras. Les dialogues et paysages sonores ainsi créés ont ensuite été traduits en une installation adaptée pour Kanal. Blindsight vous immerge dans une expérience sensorielle. Le son provient de haut-parleurs…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":0.0,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/7bb8ee2a1200abbbcc78f3e6ef2f5ecb4b5f1d91.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.596138","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-596146","title":"Joshua Serafin","category":"art","venueID":"v-a4450aabedab","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"En 1909, lʹarrière-arrière-grand-père japonais de Joshua Serafin émigre aux Philippines. Avec lʹinstallation vidéo Whispering pleas of the eternal echoes, conçue spécialement pour lʹinauguration de Kanal, on est littéralement aspiré dans une quête des origines. Dans un profond désir dʹappartenance et de connaissance du passé, Serafin réunit des personnages et des entités non physiques de différentes époques et régions du monde. Des images filmées aux Philippines alternent avec des scènes tournées en Belgique. Dans un univers entièrement créé par lʹartiste, les générations passées et actuelles se parlent comme si elles se trouvaient de part et dʹautre dʹun seuil cosmique. La pratique artistique de Joshua Serafin est centrée sur la chorégraphie et la queerness, et explore la manière dont le corps, lʹenvironnement et les publics interagissent pour créer du sens. De Manille à Hong Kong puis…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":0.0,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/1793943102854-576def287fe2e5036e707cb31c5c067826844d0b.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.596146","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-otobong-nkanga","title":"Otobong Nkanga","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-04-18T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"For the opening of Kanal, Otobong Nkanga weaves stories through threads. An installation of looms becomes the backdrop for encounters and conversations about sustainability and ownership, but also about the museum’s role in the social ecosystem.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v8yPIAQ.jpg?crop=2975%2C1556%2C0%2C2334&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/otobong-nkanga","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-596143","title":"Otobong Nkanga","category":"art","venueID":"v-a4450aabedab","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-04-18T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"À la demande de Kanal, Otobong Nkanga transforme un des vastes espaces ouverts du musée en un lieu intime de rencontre et de cocréation. Autour de métiers à tisser en bois, des participant·es sont formé·es pour l'occasion et se mettent à l’ouvrage ensemble. Compétences et expériences sont échangées. Des fils sont tissés, des récits personnels et collectifs s’entremêlent. L’acte de tisser devient un acte social, une entreprise commune qui contribue à l’œuvre finale. Dans le contexte du nouveau musée, autrefois garage automobile et immense site de production, l'installation invite à réfléchir au travail et aux structures économiques qui sous-tendent les institutions artistiques et le monde en général. Dans sa pratique artistique, Otobong Nkanga s’intéresse à la manière dont les systèmes et processus influencent les gens et les choses. En distribuant ici le travail et les ressources sur…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/7bb8ee2a1200abbbcc78f3e6ef2f5ecb4b5f1d91.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.596143","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-infinite-woman","title":"An infinite woman","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-04-25T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"A century ago, the mass-produced image of a Mangbetu woman went viral. An infinite woman explores how the distinctive profile of the Mangbetus from Congo became a modernist and colonial emblem after Citroën’s La Croisière Noire expedition, but also a powerful catalyst for artists. Through archives and works by contemporary artists like Carrie Mae Weems, Frida Orupabo and Magdalene Odundo, the exhibition celebrates the limitless Black female imagination in resisting the colonial algorithm.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003wE0rIAE.png?crop=1200%2C628%2C0%2C83&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/infinite-woman","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-596141","title":"An infinite woman","category":"art","venueID":"v-a4450aabedab","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-04-25T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"En 1925, lʹimage dʹune femme du peuple Mangbetu, dans le nord-est du Congo, est lʹemblème de la campagne de propagande pour La Croisière Noire, une expédition coloniale à travers le continent africain. Cette image de la traversée organisée par le constructeur automobile Citroën deviendra virale. En 1934, les travaux de construction du garage phare de la marque Citroën débutent à Bruxelles, créant une vitrine pour lʹautomobile autant que pour lʹidée de conquête impériale. Aujourdʹhui transformé en musée Kanal, le site ouvre ses portes avec lʹexposition An infinite woman. En deux parties, celle-ci revisite la circulation de lʹimage des femmes Mangbetu comme symbole colonial, et son renversement par les artistes afro-descendant·es qui se la sont réappropriée. Le premier acte est une recherche dans des archives qui retrace la viralité naissante des images des Mangbetus comme \"fétiches…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":0.0,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/1794838974938-086aa7b02eacc9e1d692c52603f821f1a0da15c6.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.596141","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-banu-cennetoglu","title":"Banu Cennetoğlu","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-23T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"What do human rights mean today, in a world where they continue to be undermined and violated? In right?, Banu Cennetoğlu presents the articles of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights of 1948 in bouquets of gold letter balloons in Kanal’s showroom. As the balloons slowly deflate, the work questions the language of rights and the human rights framework the Declaration helped put into place. It reflects on what these rights mean, their history and lofty rhetoric, but also on how their inherent promises visibly fade.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003vXbpIAE.jpg?crop=5239%2C2741%2C0%2C2557&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/banu-cennetoglu","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-596144","title":"Banu Cennetoğlu","category":"art","venueID":"v-a4450aabedab","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-23T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Pour right?, Banu Cennetoğlu présente la Déclaration universelle des droits de l’Homme dans le showroom de Kanal sous la forme de bouquets de lettres-ballons dorées. Chaque bouquet correspond à un des 30 articles de la Déclaration. Proclamée par l’Assemblée générale des Nations Unies à Paris le 10 décembre 1948, trois ans après la fin de la Deuxième Guerre mondiale, elle énonce pour la première fois les droits humains fondamentaux qui doivent être universellement protégés. À l’occasion de l’inauguration de Kanal, l’artiste, qui vit à Istanbul, montrera pour la première fois les 30 articles en même temps. Ce n’est pas un hasard si cela se passe à Bruxelles, siège des institutions européennes et quartier général de l’OTAN, des organisations qui affirment défendre la paix et la démocratie. Tout au long de l’exposition, les ballons se dégonflent et leur éclat se fane. Les lettres se…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/7bb8ee2a1200abbbcc78f3e6ef2f5ecb4b5f1d91.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.596144","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-right-city-right-future","title":"Right to the City - Right to the Future","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-30T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"The exhibition Right to the City – Right to the Future, organised by Kanal Architecture, presents a critical homage to Brussels, portraying Brussels as a pioneering laboratory for innovative spatial practice. As the capital of Europe, Brussels is often associated with dysfunction, bureaucracy and poor governance. The exhibition offers an alternative perspective, showing that it is paradoxically the tensions inherent to this city that have created fertile ground from which alternative practices have emerged and flourished.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000005OzdmIAC.jpg?crop=811%2C424%2C0%2C94&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/right-city-right-future","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-departement-des-pieges","title":"Département des Pièges","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-30T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"With a wink to Brussels artist Marcel Broodthaers, Clémentine Deliss invites you to enter the Département des Pièges. Here, you will find a selection of unexpected artefacts and paintings from 11 Brussels museums, as well as works by contemporary artists. From elaborate fishnets to hunting decoys, psychiatric tests and trompe l’oeil paintings, each exhibit relates to the concept of the trap. You are invited to study these diverse traps and participate in this \"museum-university\".","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v7cXIAQ.jpg?crop=7951%2C4161%2C0%2C569&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/departement-des-pieges","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-truly-immense-journey","title":"A truly immense journey","category":"art","venueID":"v-f28858adaf9a","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2028-01-09T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"A truly immense journey guides you through the forces that have set people, ideas and artistic forms in motion from the early 20th century to today. The exhibition spans modern icons such as Lygia Clark, Sonia Delaunay, Alberto Giacometti, Natalia Goncharova, Wifredo Lam and Henri Matisse, alongside contemporary international and Brussels-based artists including Sammy Baloji, Edith Dekyndt and Hana Miletić. More than 350 works, predominantly from the Centre Pompidou and Kanal, but also from numerous Belgian public and private holdings are brought together.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003vXdWIAU.jpg?crop=6454%2C3377%2C0%2C2273&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/truly-immense-journey","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-596140","title":"A truly immense journey","category":"art","venueID":"v-a4450aabedab","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2028-01-09T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"A truly immense journey vous invite à un voyage sans destination fixe, au fil des forces qui propulsent les humains, les idées et les pratiques artistiques à travers les géographies et les histoires depuis les années 1900 jusquʹà aujourdʹhui. Plus de 350 œuvres dʹart provenant en grande majorité du Centre Pompidou, de Kanal mais également dʹautres collections publiques et privées belges sont présentées dans lʹexposition. On y chemine entre pays et mouvements, à la rencontre dʹicônes de lʹart moderne comme Lygia Clark, Sonia Delaunay, Natalia Gontcharova, Henri Matisse, Wifredo Lam, Katarzyna Kobro, Pablo Picasso ou Alberto Giacometti et dʹartistes contemporain·es de la scène bruxelloise et internationale, comme Sammy Baloji, Edith Dekyndt, Aglaia Konrad et Hana Miletić. La combinaison dʹœuvres historiques et contemporaines crée des constellations surprenantes qui jettent une lumière…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":0.0,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/1793943098445-0efb2449ec6dcfc939fd0bd1961a80fb17cb924f.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.596140","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2110-mole-carla-manrique-mendoza","title":"MOLE","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-28T17:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-29T20:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Une femme dans sa chambre. Elle a décidé d'en finir. Son Opinel n'est pas assez aiguisé, le miroir Ikea refuse de se casser, et le numéro anti-suicide ne répond pas. La mort ne joue pas le jeu ce soir-là.\r\n\r\nAutour de ce ratage fondateur, Carla Margarita…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/activity/2110","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2110-mole-carla-manrique-mendoza","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-les-halles-de-schaer-2111-le-shit-show-x-anal-pompidou","title":"Le Shit Show x Anal Pompidou","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w1026048575","start":"2026-11-28T19:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-28T22:00:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Le cabaret marseillais de haut vol Shit Show s'installe aux Halles de Schaerbeek pour clore en beauté la première édition du festival Cuddles. Mémorable !","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/image/og/image/4482","sourceURL":"https://www.halles.be/fr/ap/2111-le-shit-show-x-anal-pompidou","sourceName":"Les Halles de Schaerbeek","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700028997","title":"La Cambre 100 ANS! - 100 GESTES","category":"art","venueID":"v-3cba1f940a72","start":"2026-11-29T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-01-30T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Le premier ensemble est né d’un exercice proposé par Stéphanie Mahieu à ses étudiant·e·s de Bachelier 3 en Anthropologie de l’art au printemps 2026. Il réunit 37 objets choisis par chacun·e, accompagnés d’un texte qui en révèle l’histoire, l’usage ou la valeur particulière. Loin de constituer un inventaire ordonné, cette sélection compose une constellation de choses apparemment disparates, reliées par les récits et les regards de celles et ceux qui les ont choisies. Certains objets sont directement liés aux pratiques de l’école : un tablier de sérigraphie, un serre-joint de textile, des outils familiers qui portent la trace des gestes et des savoir-faire. D’autres renvoient à leur inscription dans un lieu et dans une histoire : éléments architecturaux, ascenseurs, cartes postales évoquant La Cambre avant sa transformation en école d’art. D’autres encore appartiennent à une dimension…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/caefdf500975eba57495ca7eaa6372217e89535d.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700028997","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":false,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"stage-kaaitheater-ecopolis","title":"ECOPOLIS","category":"theatre","venueID":"v-d917fd6e2961","start":"2026-12-04T23:00:59Z","end":"2026-12-05T22:59:59Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"On December 5, ECOPOLIS, Fair(er) Futures Festival will once again bring together thinkers and doers, writers, artists, and activists from various countries for a day filled with inspiring conversations, hopeful ideas, and new perspectives.After all, we live in a time of great challenges: think of climate disruption and growing inequality. This raises numerous questions. How do we build a future that works for everyone again? And what do we need to envision—and also shape—that future?We ask the big questions—such as the one posed by Anna Tsing: What is the art of living on a damaged planet?…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.kaaitheater.be/sites/default/files/26-27/Unknown-4.png","sourceURL":"https://www.kaaitheater.be/en/agenda/26-27/ecopolis","sourceName":"Kaaitheater","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700028689","title":"Crush","category":"theatre","venueID":"osm-w256394182","start":"2026-12-08T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-12-12T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"CRUSH — la nouvelle biennale de théâtre à Bruxelles — se tiendra du 9 au 12 décembre 2026 aux Théâtre Les Tanneurs, Théâtre National Wallonie-Bruxelles, Théâtre le Rideau et Varia – Théâtre & Studio. Quatre jours pour découvrir nos onze coups de cœur de la création théâtrale en Fédération Wallonie-Bruxelles. Né de la volonté de nos quatre maisons bruxelloises de mettre en commun nos regards et sensibilités, le festival CRUSH met en lumière des spectacles belges francophones marquants, portés par des esthétiques plurielles et des voix singulières. L’enjeu est clair : offrir aux artistes et aux œuvres un espace de déploiement ambitieux, créer les conditions d’une véritable circulation — des spectacles, des idées, des imaginaires — et favoriser la rencontre avec de nouveaux publics, en Belgique et au-delà. Pour les spectateur·ices, des parcours vous permettent de circuler d’un théâtre à…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":10.0,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/e4fcff394d0782dfde958e905e3f7aeacdfdbc3c.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700028689","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700029136